# Named, tracked CVE exceptions for the zero-tolerance "container image →
# ghcr.io" CVE scan gate (release.yml's `cve-scan` job,
# pleme-io/actions/image-scan@main, fail-on-severity: UNKNOWN). Every entry
# here MUST carry its own justification — this file is never a substitute
# for actually fixing what can be fixed. Style + discipline mirrored from
# pleme-io/hardened-images' own .trivyignore (the sibling initiative that
# established this pattern for the fleet). Re-check each entry whenever its
# package's upstream releases a newer version.
#
# Ground truth for every entry below: a real `trivy image --format json`
# scan of ghcr.io/pleme-io/pangea-operator:embedded-amd64-r166-96fa855c65
# (run 29698809855, 2026-07-19) — 267 total findings, 10 CRITICAL. That scan
# is the FIRST time this gate ever actually evaluated a real image (a
# substring-match bug in the old gate code silently no-op'd it since it was
# added — fixed pleme-io/actions commit 2026-07-17, two days before this
# run). The 6 opentofu/packer/terraform-provider CRITICALs fixed by this
# same commit's flake.nix change (opentofu, packer, terraform-provider-
# github/-cloudflare/-aws/-kubernetes bumped via a nixpkgs-security escape
# hatch) are NOT listed here — they're closed for real, not ignorefile'd.

# --- pangea-compiler embedded Ruby gemset -------------------------------
# net-imap 0.4.21 (bundled gem, installed by ruby_3_3's own upstream build,
# NOT a Gemfile.lock dependency — confirmed via direct inspection of the
# substituted x86_64-linux ruby_3_3 store path:
# lib/ruby/gems/3.3.0/{specifications,gems,cache}/net-imap-0.4.21.*).
# Ruby 3.3.12 (released 2026-07-16, 3 days before this scan) bumps the
# bundled net-imap to 0.4.25, closing all 8 of these — but no nixpkgs
# channel has packaged 3.3.12 yet as of 2026-07-19 (confirmed: nixpkgs
# nixos-unstable @ 61b7c44, the tip of the branch at scan time, still
# ships ruby_3_3 == 3.3.10). A real fix exists and is fully scoped: a
# `ruby_3_3.overrideAttrs` `postFixup` file-swap (net-imap is pure Ruby,
# no C extension — the same technique pleme-io/hardened-images uses for
# Neo4j's jackson-databind jars) replacing the net-imap-0.4.21 gem tree +
# gemspec + cache entry with the real published net-imap-0.4.25.gem
# (paths verified against the real store layout above). NOT applied here:
# unlike Neo4j's jar swap (unpack a tarball, no compile), overriding
# ruby_3_3 forces Nix to treat it as a new derivation and recompile the
# WHOLE Ruby interpreter from source — no reachable x86_64-linux builder
# from this workstation to verify that build succeeds and Ruby still
# boots correctly afterward before shipping it blind. Named, scoped
# follow-up, not swept under the rug.
CVE-2026-42257
CVE-2026-42245
CVE-2026-42246
CVE-2026-42256
CVE-2026-42258
CVE-2026-47240
CVE-2026-47242
CVE-2026-47241

# erb 4.0.3 (ruby_3_3's own default gem, loaded from the CORE stdlib path
# lib/ruby/3.3.0/erb.rb — confirmed via direct inspection, ahead of any
# gem search path). Fixed at 4.0.3.1 by ruby 3.3.12 (same release as
# net-imap above, same "no nixpkgs channel has it yet" blocker). The
# standalone `erb` gem on rubygems.org has diverged onto its own 6.0.x
# version line (unrelated to ruby's internal 4.0.x bundled-gem numbering);
# trivy's own fix range (">= 6.0.4") confirms 6.0.x is an eligible
# replacement, but swapping ruby's CORE stdlib erb.rb carries real
# behavioral-compat risk (this file is loaded ahead of any gem override,
# by more of the ruby runtime than a leaf gem like net-imap) that this
# pass had no way to verify — whether any pangea-* gem in this image's own
# closure uses ERB templating was not audited, and there is no reachable
# builder to test a swap even if the API is compatible. Same underlying
# fix mechanism as net-imap (a ruby_3_3 postFixup override once nixpkgs
# ships 3.3.12, or a verified core-lib file swap) — named follow-up.
CVE-2026-41316

# zlib 3.1.1 (ruby_3_3's own default gem — a C EXTENSION wrapping libz,
# confirmed via the compiled lib/ruby/3.3.0/x86_64-linux/zlib.so alongside
# the gem's Ruby wrapper). Fixed >= 3.2.3. Ruby 3.3.12 does NOT bump zlib
# (checked its own release notes directly — only erb + net-imap are
# named). Unlike net-imap/erb, a fix here requires actually RECOMPILING
# the C extension against the newer zlib gem's ext/ source (extconf.rb +
# make), not a pure-file swap — meaningfully more involved than either
# Ruby-only case above and not attempted blind with no reachable builder
# to verify the compiled artifact still loads. Genuinely narrow exposure:
# the advisory is specifically in Zlib::GzipReader, which nothing in this
# image's own operator code path calls.
CVE-2026-27820

# --- magma provider mirror: terraform-provider-random / -porkbun / -rabbitmq
# All three verified 2026-07-19 to have NO newer upstream release on any
# channel — `gh api repos/<owner>/<repo>/releases/latest` returns the
# SAME version already packaged (random 3.9.0, porkbun 0.3.0, rabbitmq
# 1.10.1), and a direct check of each repo's go.mod at its default-branch
# HEAD (i.e. even unreleased work) still pins the same vulnerable
# google.golang.org/grpc (porkbun: v1.67.1, rabbitmq: v1.72.1 — both well
# below the 1.79.3 fix line for CVE-2026-33186). terraform-provider-porkbun
# additionally does not exist at all as a nixpkgs attribute on the
# nixpkgs-security escape-hatch pin (nixos-unstable), confirmed via a
# direct `nix eval` failure ("attribute 'porkbun' missing") — there is no
# channel this provider could be sourced from even if a newer nixpkgs
# packaging existed. Bumping ANY of these three to close their CVEs would
# require a from-scratch go.mod/go.sum patch (bumping grpc-go and, for
# random, also golang.org/x/crypto + x/net + x/text + the Go toolchain
# itself) with a real vendorHash recompute — unverifiable from this
# workstation with no reachable x86_64-linux builder, and materially
# riskier than a version bump (a wrong vendorHash or a subtly incompatible
# grpc-go pin breaks the whole provider's RPC handshake with magma at
# runtime, not just at scan time). These three provider derivations are
# left on the ORIGINAL (fleet-anchored) nixpkgs pin, unchanged by this
# commit's nixpkgs-security escape hatch.
CVE-2026-33186

