# CLOSED 2026-08-13 — packer's containerd + mongo-driver entries are DELETED,
# not moved. They suppressed six findings against packer 1.15.4:
# containerd/v2 v2.2.4 (CVE-2026-53488/-53489/-53492 HIGH,
# CVE-2026-47262/-50195 MEDIUM) and mongo-driver v1.14.0 (CVE-2026-2303).
#
# The entry's own blocker was "the fix is on packer's main but not yet in a
# tagged release, and there is no reachable x86_64-linux builder from this
# workstation to verify an untagged build". Both halves have since dissolved:
# packer cut v1.16.0, the image took it via packer-grpc-bump, and `ssh rio`
# is a 32-core x86_64-linux builder that has now built this exact derivation
# three times today.
#
# Verified against the SHIPPED BINARY, not a manifest: `go version -m` on
# /nix/store/4v956dzk85lb4sngsz8ysl2p53ljvmc8-packer-1.16.0/bin/packer reports
# containerd/v2 v2.3.3 (every fix line is 2.3.2) and NO mongo-driver module at
# all across its 410 dep lines.
#
# ONE HONEST GAP: "no OTHER binary in the image carries a vulnerable
# containerd or mongo-driver" is a closure inference — nobody has run trivy
# against r314+. The next scan is the confirmation, and it is cheap: if any of
# the six is still live the gate goes red and this deletion is one revert.
# That is the correct direction to be wrong in.

